("M-01","Major","Pre-authenticated X.509 principal extraction takes the whole subject DN through `SubjectDnX509PrincipalExtractor`, whose default pattern lifts the CN by regular expression rather than reading a fixed X.500 attribute or a SAN.","`AcmBasicAndTokenAuthenticationFilter.java:219`, imported at `:44`; whole file byte-identical to the base commit",D,"AAP 0.2.2 freezes security outcomes. The file is byte-identical to `c8f6226105`, and the API the published fix relies on, `SubjectX500PrincipalExtractor`, does not exist in Spring Security 5.8.x — it arrives in the 6.5 line, which the jakarta exclusion bars.","[Pre-existing Defects](pre-existing-defects.md) entry 100 (`S7-X509-1`); [Backend Dependency Security](backend-dependency-security.md) Finding 2","Adopt a strict fixed X.500 attribute or SAN policy, or retire the X.509 path. Both change an authentication outcome."),
