("M-04","Major","The STOMP channel interceptor logs a SUBSCRIBE frame and authorizes nothing, and the destinations are global, so any authenticated session can subscribe to any topic.","`…/websockets/AcmWebSocketChannelInterceptor.java`",D,"AAP 0.2.2 freezes security outcomes and wire behaviour. Adding destination rules changes which subscriptions succeed. Outside the 0.4.1 file list.","[Pre-existing Defects](pre-existing-defects.md) entry 31 (`S7-WS1`)","Add authenticated per-destination authorization rules and apply the Spring messaging patches, then re-test every live subscription."),
("M-05","Major","Caller-selected identifiers reach file download and seven object controllers without an ownership or object-ACL check, so a caller can name another principal's object.","`…/ecm/web/api/FileDownloadAPIController.java:56-57`; `ListBillingInvoicesAPIController.java` and six siblings",D,"AAP 0.2.2 freezes permission-evaluation outcomes explicitly. Outside the 0.4.1 file list. R-6 applies.","[Pre-existing Defects](pre-existing-defects.md) entries 22 (`S7-AUTH1`) and 30 (`S7-OBJ1`)","Resolve every identifier under the authenticated principal and enforce the object ACL in the service layer rather than the controller."),
("M-06","Major","Null-session, token-in-query and ACL-disable modes let route protection be weakened by client input or configuration, so the interceptor and permission evaluator do not fail closed.","plugin interceptor, permission evaluator and external authentication chains",D,"AAP 0.8.1 states in terms that `ArkPermissionEvaluator.java:27` **and the reflection-based scanning it depends on are unchanged**. This is the most explicit freeze in the plan and it names the component this finding targets.","[Pre-existing Defects](pre-existing-defects.md) entry 66 (`S7-AUTH2`)","Make each mode fail closed independently of client input and of configuration. This changes permission-evaluation outcomes, which the plan preserves, so it needs an explicit AAP revision."),
("M-07","Major","Decrypted configuration is serialized to the browser and a stored credential is returned by an admin GET, and CMIS property values are written to the log.","`…/config/…/web/api/ConfigApiController.java:64-72`; `EmailSenderConfigurationAPIController.java`",D,"AAP 0.2.2 freezes REST response shapes; a redacted DTO changes a response body. Outside the 0.4.1 file list.","[Pre-existing Defects](pre-existing-defects.md) entries 27 (`S7-SECRET1`) and 28 (`S7-SECRET2`)","Introduce redacted DTOs for the affected endpoints and remove secret values from log statements, then rotate anything already exposed."),
