("M-22","Major","Five test classes and one test Spring context covering the changed LDAP and Angular-copier boundaries were deleted, removing 40 tests; and the six PowerMock-to-Mockito rewrites were said to weaken error and constructor assertions.","`acm-service-login/…/ad/*Test.java` (4); `AngularResourceCopierWiringTest.java`; `angular-starter-wiring-test-context.xml`",P,"The deletions are a real regression and are restored — R-5 forbids removing coverage. The assertion half is deferred: the assertion, `@Test` and `catch` counts in all six rewritten classes are **byte-identical to `c8f6226105`**, so the vacuous blocks are pre-migration source, and strengthening them would modify existing test assertions, which AAP 0.2.2 preserves.","this page, and the restored files themselves","Authorise strengthening the pre-existing vacuous `catch` blocks in the six rewritten classes if the weak assertions matter. That is a change to existing test assertions and needs an AAP revision."),
