("N-10","Minor","Five production reflection sites use the deprecated `Class.newInstance()`, which propagates a constructor-thrown checked exception without wrapping it.","`AcmObjectUtilsImpl.java:63-64`; `CorrespondenceServiceImpl.java:371`; `ArkPermissionEvaluator.java:514`; `AcmParticipantService.java:240`; `CamelContextManager.java:208`",D,"One of the five is `ArkPermissionEvaluator.java`, which AAP 0.8.1 freezes by name together with the reflection-based scanning it depends on. For all five, the replacement changes the exception a constructor failure surfaces as — from an undeclared checked exception to `InvocationTargetException` — which is an observable behaviour change with no JDK 17 compatibility reason: all five compile and run at release 17.","[Pre-existing Defects](pre-existing-defects.md) entry 109 (`I13`)","Replace with `getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance()` and handle `InvocationTargetException` at each call site. Requires an AAP revision for the permission-evaluator site."),
